			<small class="meta">May 15th, 2007 </small>

			<div class="entry">
				<p>&nbsp;Every now and again I find a tool that changes my life.&nbsp; <a href="http://www.baremetalsoft.com/baretail/">Baretail</a>&nbsp;is just such a tool.&nbsp; I don&#8217;t know what I did before, but it couldn&#8217;t have been good.&nbsp; Baretail is a log file reader/watcher that trails the end of your log files.&nbsp; This may not be too exciting for you, but here in the <a href="http://www.speedway.com/speedyrewards/">Speedy Rewards</a>&nbsp;team, we have some terribly verbose 3rd party log files that are our only real insight into activity.&nbsp; This has made my week!</p>
<p><a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/blogs/ryanc/WindowsLiveWriter/AwesomeTooloftheDayBaretail_8BB6/baretail-screencap%5B1%5D.png" atomicselection="true"><img style="border-right: 0px; border-top: 0px; border-left: 0px; border-bottom: 0px" height="343" src="http://cromwellhaus.com/blogs/ryanc/WindowsLiveWriter/AwesomeTooloftheDayBaretail_8BB6/baretail-screencap_thumb%5B1%5D.png" width="425" border="0"></a></p>
